          <!-- ===== TAB 6 : TROUBLESHOOTING ===== -->
          <div class="tab-pane fade p-4" id="tab-trouble" role="tabpanel">
            <div class="alert alert-primary py-2 small mb-3">
              <i class="fas fa-info-circle me-1"></i>
              <strong>Before escalating:</strong> (1) Refresh the page. (2) Log out &amp; log back in. (3) Clear browser cache. (4) Try a different browser. If the issue persists after these steps, escalate via your configured channel.
            </div>
            <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-3">
              <div class="card-header py-2 small fw-bold text-uppercase bg-danger text-white">Troubleshooting Matrix</div>
              <div class="card-body p-0">
                <table class="table table-sm sop-table mb-0">
                  <thead>
                    <tr>
                      <th style="width:20%">Issue / Symptom</th>
                      <th style="width:10%">Severity</th>
                      <th style="width:24%">Likely Cause(s)</th>
                      <th style="width:30%">Resolution Steps</th>
                      <th style="width:16%">Role Required</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Payment button disabled / greyed out</strong></td>
                      <td><span class="badge badge-severity-med" style="background:#fd7e14;">MEDIUM</span></td>
                      <td>Order not saved, no items added, or no items fired</td>
                      <td>1. Add &amp; save items (<span class="kbd-pill">Ctrl+S</span>)<br/>2. Fire items (<span class="kbd-pill">Ctrl+F</span>)<br/>3. Refresh page if still blocked</td>
                      <td>Cashier</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Day Closing blocked / Lock button disabled</strong></td>
                      <td><span class="badge badge-severity-high" style="background:#dc3545;">HIGH</span></td>
                      <td>Open orders exist, variance exceeds threshold, or previous day not locked</td>
                      <td>1. Settle all open orders<br/>2. Verify cash count matches system expected<br/>3. Manager approves variance if acceptable<br/>4. If previous day open, lock it first</td>
                      <td>Manager</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>BOT ticket stuck "In Progress"</strong></td>
                      <td><span class="badge badge-severity-med" style="background:#fd7e14;">MEDIUM</span></td>
                      <td>Bar staff did not click Mark Ready on BOT Dashboard</td>
                      <td>1. Open BOT Dashboard<br/>2. Locate the ticket<br/>3. Click <em>Mark Ready</em><br/>4. Cashier then marks Billed after payment</td>
                      <td>Bar Staff / Manager</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>KOT ticket not received in kitchen</strong></td>
                      <td><span class="badge badge-severity-high" style="background:#dc3545;">HIGH</span></td>
                      <td>Order not fired, network issue, or KDS not connected</td>
                      <td>1. Confirm order is in FIRED status on POS<br/>2. Check KDS network connection<br/>3. Refresh KDS page<br/>4. If urgent, take manual order slip to kitchen</td>
                      <td>Cashier/IT</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Print bill fails / blank receipt</strong></td>
                      <td><span class="badge badge-severity-med" style="background:#fd7e14;">MEDIUM</span></td>
                      <td>Bill not generated, printer offline, or browser popup blocked</td>
                      <td>1. Ensure payment was settled (order status = COMPLETED)<br/>2. Check printer is online and paper loaded<br/>3. Allow pop-ups for this site in browser settings<br/>4. Re-open the order and use the Print button</td>
                      <td>Cashier</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Email not sending (bill / reset password)</strong></td>
                      <td><span class="badge badge-severity-med" style="background:#fd7e14;">MEDIUM</span></td>
                      <td>SMTP config missing, inactive, or wrong credentials</td>
                      <td>1. Go to <em>Settings → Mail Configuration</em><br/>2. Verify host, port, username, password, SSL settings<br/>3. Click <em>Test Email</em> to validate<br/>4. Ensure config is marked <em>Active</em> and linked to the branch</td>
                      <td>Admin</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Missing data in reports</strong></td>
                      <td><span class="badge badge-severity-low" style="background:#198754;">LOW</span></td>
                      <td>Day not locked, wrong date range, or wrong branch selected</td>
                      <td>1. Check date range filter in report<br/>2. Verify branch selector matches expected branch<br/>3. Complete Day Closing and lock the day<br/>4. Re-generate report after lock</td>
                      <td>Manager</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Discount approval loop (can't settle)</strong></td>
                      <td><span class="badge badge-severity-med" style="background:#fd7e14;">MEDIUM</span></td>
                      <td>Discount exceeds configured limit; waiting for manager token</td>
                      <td>1. Manager must be physically present<br/>2. Open approval prompt and enter manager credentials<br/>3. Alternatively, reduce discount to within auto-approve limit</td>
                      <td>Manager</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Login slow / branch select slow</strong></td>
                      <td><span class="badge badge-severity-low" style="background:#198754;">LOW</span></td>
                      <td>First login after server restart (cache warming), slow network</td>
                      <td>1. First login is slower due to schema cache warm-up (normal)<br/>2. Subsequent logins in same session will be fast (30-min cache)<br/>3. For persistent slowness, check server resources with IT</td>
                      <td>IT</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Hotkey not working</strong></td>
                      <td><span class="badge badge-severity-low" style="background:#198754;">LOW</span></td>
                      <td>Input field focused, wrong page context, or browser override</td>
                      <td>1. Click in an empty area of the page to deselect any input<br/>2. Verify you are on the correct page (see Hotkeys tab)<br/>3. Check browser isn't intercepting the shortcut (e.g., Ctrl+F in some browsers)</td>
                      <td>Cashier</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Order shows wrong table / section</strong></td>
                      <td><span class="badge badge-severity-med" style="background:#fd7e14;">MEDIUM</span></td>
                      <td>Table was assigned on create but not updated after guest move</td>
                      <td>1. Open order details<br/>2. Use <em>Transfer Table</em> option<br/>3. Select correct table<br/>4. Save; Table Dashboard updates automatically</td>
                      <td>Waiter / Cashier</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>GST not showing on bill</strong></td>
                      <td><span class="badge badge-severity-med" style="background:#fd7e14;">MEDIUM</span></td>
                      <td>GST rates not configured on Menu Items</td>
                      <td>1. Go to <em>Menu → Item Master</em><br/>2. Edit the item and set CGST / SGST rates<br/>3. Future orders will reflect the correct GST<br/><em>Note: Historical orders cannot be retroactively updated.</em></td>
                      <td>Admin / Manager</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td><strong>Cannot void / cancel order</strong></td>
                      <td><span class="badge badge-severity-high" style="background:#dc3545;">HIGH</span></td>
                      <td>Order already COMPLETED (payment settled), or day locked</td>
                      <td>1. If order is paid, it cannot be voided — issue a refund manually<br/>2. If day locked, contact system admin<br/>3. For unfired orders: Delete directly from order details page</td>
                      <td>Manager / Admin</td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- ===== TAB 7 : SETTINGS & ADMIN ===== -->
          <div class="tab-pane fade p-4" id="tab-admin" role="tabpanel">
            <div class="row g-3">
              <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-3">
                  <div class="card-header py-2 small fw-bold text-uppercase bg-dark text-white">Initial Setup Checklist (New Deployment)</div>
                  <div class="card-body p-3">
                    <ol class="sop-list ps-0 mb-0 list-unstyled">
                      <div class="sop-step"><strong>Branch &amp; Organisation Setup</strong><br/><span class="text-muted small">Settings → Branches: Add branch name, address, GSTIN, contact. Assign the branch to all users.</span></div>
                      <div class="sop-step"><strong>User Roles</strong><br/><span class="text-muted small">Admin → Users: Create accounts for Manager, Cashier, Kitchen, Bar Staff. Assign correct roles &amp; branch(es).</span></div>
                      <div class="sop-step"><strong>Menu Structure</strong><br/><span class="text-muted small">Masters → Categories → SubCategories → Items. Set GST rates, prices, kitchen station, and UOM per item.</span></div>
                      <div class="sop-step"><strong>Table Layout</strong><br/><span class="text-muted small">Settings → Tables &amp; Sections: Create sections (e.g., Ground Floor, Rooftop) and assign tables with capacity.</span></div>
                      <div class="sop-step"><strong>Kitchen Stations</strong><br/><span class="text-muted small">Settings → Kitchen Stations: Create stations and link menu items for intelligent KOT routing.</span></div>
                      <div class="sop-step"><strong>Payment Configuration</strong><br/><span class="text-muted small">Settings → Payment Modes: Enable Cash, UPI, Card, etc. Configure discount thresholds and GST number.</span></div>
                      <div class="sop-step"><strong>Mail Configuration</strong><br/><span class="text-muted small">Settings → Mail Config: Enter SMTP details. Click Test to verify. Link config to branch. Required for bill email &amp; password reset.</span></div>
                      <div class="sop-step sop-check"><strong>Day Closing Thresholds</strong><br/><span class="text-muted small">Settings → Day Closing: Set variance tolerance (₹ or %) above which manager approval is mandatory before locking.</span></div>
                    </ol>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-3">
                  <div class="card-header py-2 small fw-bold text-uppercase" style="background:#e8f0fe;">User &amp; Role Management</div>
