          <div class="tab-pane fade p-4" id="tab-faq" role="tabpanel">
            <div class="row g-3">
              <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm h-100">
                  <div class="card-header py-2 small fw-bold text-uppercase bg-primary text-white">Operations FAQ</div>
                  <div class="card-body p-3">
                    <div class="accordion accordion-flush" id="faqOpsAccordion">
                      <div class="accordion-item border-bottom">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq1">Can I add items to an order after it has been fired?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faq1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqOpsAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">Yes. Add new items to the order and press <span class="kbd-pill">Ctrl+F</span> again. Only the <em>newly added, un-fired items</em> will be sent to kitchen/bar. Previously fired items are not re-sent, so there is no duplication risk.</div></div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="accordion-item border-bottom">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq2">What happens if I forget to open the float?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqOpsAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">You can still create and process orders, but the Cash Closing Report will show Opening Balance as ₹0, causing a closing variance equal to the actual float amount. Always open float before the first order. If missed, a manager can manually adjust the opening balance before day lock.</div></div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="accordion-item border-bottom">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq3">Can I reopen a locked business day?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqOpsAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">No. Day lock is a permanent financial control measure. Once locked, no orders or payments for that day can be modified. If an error was made, it must be corrected in the next available business day as an adjustment, documented with proper reason.</div></div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="accordion-item border-bottom">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq4">How do I handle a split bill between two guests?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqOpsAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">On the Payment screen, click <em>Split Payment</em>. Allocate the amount per payment mode or enter amounts for each payer. The total of all splits must equal the bill total. Each split is recorded independently in the Collection Register.</div></div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="accordion-item border-bottom">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq5">Why can't I see my menu items in the order?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faq5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqOpsAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">Menu items may be marked <em>Inactive</em> or not assigned to the current branch. Check <em>Menu → Item Master</em>: ensure the item is Active and linked to the correct branch. Items in inactive categories are also hidden.</div></div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="accordion-item border-bottom">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq6">Can a cashier process a refund?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faq6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqOpsAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">Paid orders cannot be modified. Refunds are handled as a manual cash adjustment (give cash back) and must be documented by the manager. Record the refund reason in the next available order log or as a negative adjustment note during Day Closing variance explanation.</div></div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq7">How is GST calculated on discounted bills?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faq7" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqOpsAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">Discount is applied to the base (pre-tax) item price first. GST is then calculated on the discounted taxable value. This follows the standard GST net-pricing methodology. Example: ₹500 item – ₹50 discount = ₹450 taxable value → GST applied on ₹450.</div></div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm h-100">
                  <div class="card-header py-2 small fw-bold text-uppercase" style="background:#e2d9f3; color:#4e17c7;">Technical &amp; Admin FAQ</div>
                  <div class="card-body p-3">
                    <div class="accordion accordion-flush" id="faqTechAccordion">
                      <div class="accordion-item border-bottom">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqt1">Why is first login slow after a server restart?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faqt1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqTechAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">On first login after a restart, the system performs branch schema detection (checking ~13 database features). Results are cached for 30 minutes. Subsequent logins within the cache window are immediate. This is normal and expected behaviour.</div></div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="accordion-item border-bottom">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqt2">How do I set up email for bill delivery?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faqt2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqTechAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">1. Go to <em>Settings → Mail Configuration</em>. 2. Enter SMTP server, port, username, password. 3. Enable SSL/TLS as per your provider. 4. Click <em>Test Email</em> to confirm delivery. 5. Mark the config Active and link it to the branch. Guest email field on the order must be populated to trigger bill email.</div></div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="accordion-item border-bottom">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqt3">How do I switch my active branch or role?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faqt3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqTechAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">Use the Branch / Role switcher in the top navigation bar. Switching branch re-scopes all dashboards, orders, and reports to the selected branch. Switching role changes your permissions within the same branch. A brief page reload occurs after switching.</div></div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="accordion-item border-bottom">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqt4">What data does the Transaction Cleanup script delete?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faqt4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqTechAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">The <code>_dependency_safe</code> script deletes: Orders, OrderItems, Payments, KOT/BOT Tickets, Day Closing records, Feedback, Email Logs, Loyalty Transactions, and all related child tables — in FK-safe order using DELETE (not TRUNCATE). Master data (Menu, Tables, Users, Settings) is <strong>never touched</strong>. A full cleanup + date-range mode is supported.</div></div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="accordion-item border-bottom">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqt5">Can I run the system on multiple devices simultaneously?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faqt5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqTechAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">Yes. The system is web-based and supports concurrent users. Each user logs in with their own credentials. Use separate user accounts (not shared credentials) to maintain audit trail integrity. Kitchen and BOT displays can be open on dedicated tablets or monitors without affecting POS performance.</div></div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="accordion-item border-bottom">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqt6">How do I prevent an item from appearing on the menu QR?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faqt6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqTechAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">Mark the item as <em>Inactive</em> in <em>Menu → Item Master</em>. Inactive items do not appear on the digital menu QR page, in search results on the POS, or in new order item selection. They remain visible in historical reports and orders.</div></div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header"><button class="accordion-button collapsed py-2 faq-q" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqt7">How are loyalty points accumulated and redeemed?</button></h2>
                        <div id="faqt7" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqTechAccordion"><div class="accordion-body py-2 faq-a">Points accumulate per order based on the configured earning rate (e.g., 1 point per ₹100 spent). On the payment screen, if a guest card number is entered and sufficient points exist, a redemption option appears. Redemption is applied as a discount before GST. All transactions log to <code>GuestLoyaltyTransaction</code> for audit.</div></div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div><!-- /.tab-content -->
